## Story Description
[Mozio] - The Promo code amount is NOT displayed as expected for Return trip tickets in the Mozio email confirmation

## Acceptance Criteria
- The function promoAppliesToLineItem in src/services/mozio/email-promo-discount.ts MUST return true when a valid promo object is passed and the line item represents a return trip (i.e., has a dateFrom and dateTo indicating a round trip), ensuring the promo is evaluated for both outbound and return legs.
- The Mozio email confirmation template MUST render the promo code discount amount for the return trip portion of a round-trip ticket when a promo code is applied, matching the format used for the outbound trip.
- The test suite for src/services/mozio/email-promo-discount.ts MUST include a test case that passes a valid promo object and a return-trip line item to promoAppliesToLineItem and asserts a true return value.
- The test suite for src/services/mozio/email-promo-discount.ts MUST NOT omit a test case that passes null or undefined as the promo argument to promoAppliesToLineItem and asserts a false return value (rule: no-coverage). Verify with: grep -rn 'promoAppliesToLineItem' test/ --include='*.ts' | grep -E 'null|undefined' | wc -l — result must be ≥ 1.
- The function promoAppliesToLineItem in src/services/mozio/email-promo-discount.ts MUST NOT return a truthy value when the promo argument is null or undefined (rule: no-coverage). Verify with: node -e "const m=require('./src/services/mozio/email-promo-discount'); process.exit(m.promoAppliesToLineItem(null)===false && m.promoAppliesToLineItem(undefined)===false ? 0 : 1)" — exit code must be 0.
- The email confirmation generation MUST include the promo discount amount line item for the return trip when a promo code is applied to a round-trip order, and the rendered output must be verifiable via a snapshot or assertion-based test.

